# Review ownership. GitHub requests a review from the owner automatically on
# every pull request touching a matching path.
#
# Ownership is stated per area rather than with one blanket rule, so that
# handing over an area later is a one-line edit naming the successor. The areas
# are the ones where a change can be silently wrong: the scoring engine, the
# compiled kernels, the tests that are the only proof the scores are right, the
# sync-time contract, and the invariants themselves.
#
# NOTE: a CODEOWNERS entry only requests a review. It does not require one until
# branch protection on main turns on "Require review from Code Owners", which
# needs a repository admin to enable once.

*                   @hhp94

/R/                 @hhp94
/src/               @hhp94
/tests/             @hhp94
/data-raw/          @hhp94
/.claude/           @hhp94
/.github/           @hhp94
/DESCRIPTION        @hhp94
/NAMESPACE          @hhp94
